  "answer": "This has been requested before: Keyboard Manager remaps apply globally to all keyboards, so remapping or disabling a key on a faulty laptop keyboard also affects the external one. Per-keyboard remapping (internal vs. external) is an open feature request in #48312 and #48310, and #41320 asks for the same thing (apply to built-in or external keyboard). None of these tickets offers a built-in fix yet. The workaround described in #41320 is to toggle Keyboard Manager off when using the external keyboard and on when using the built-in one. Please add your use case (faulty internal keyboard) to those tickets rather than opening a new one."
